{"id": 51, "ts": 1780502126.6527576, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I remain aligned with James in recommending Candidate\u202fB as the provisional hire, conditional on a focused communication\u2011development plan.\u202fWhile Candidate\u202fA brings strong technical foresight \u2013 he \u201canticipates dangerous situations,\u201d \u201csees complex connections,\u201d and has \u201cvery good leadership qualities\u201d \u2013 his noted unfriendly demeanor and unhealthy habits raise red flags for crew cooperation and long\u2011term reliability, which we have no concrete evidence to offset.\u202fCandidate\u202fD, on the other hand, \u201ctakes responsibility seriously\u201d and \u201cconcentrates very well,\u201d yet the same notes describe him as **arrogant**, with **relatively weak leadership skills** and a **hot temper**, and we still lack any observation of his stress\u2011resilience or crew\u2011cooperation.\u202fGiven that B already demonstrates the core safety\u2011critical criteria we need \u2013 \u201cvery conscientious\u201d (operational reliability), \u201chandles stress very well\u201d (stress resilience), and solid technical competence (weather assessment, computer skills) \u2013 the communication issue is the only remaining concern and is addressable through training.\u202fTherefore, I vote for Candidate\u202fB, while urging that we obtain at least one concrete example of A\u2019s reliability or D\u2019s stress handling before closing the decision."}
